From 6aef763297e6348412e62e824452c4fbd657c44a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Chong <achong@meta.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Apr 2026 12:51:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 57/63] [cuttlefish host-tools] pass --vhost_user_vsock to
 rootcanal and netsim proxies

Summary:
## Problem

On macOS, `socket_vsock_proxy` instances launched for Root Canal
(Bluetooth HCI/test ports 7300/7500) and netsim fail with:

```
Unrecoverable vsock server error - Port: 7500, vhost-user CID: none,
Error: Operation not supported by device (errno: 19)
```

macOS has no native `AF_VSOCK` kernel driver. When `--vhost_user_vsock`
is not passed, the proxy calls `socket(AF_VSOCK, SOCK_STREAM, 0)` which
returns `ENODEV` (errno 19). With the flag, it uses a Unix domain socket
path instead (`/tmp/vsock_<cid>_<uid>/vm.vsock_<port>`).

The ADB proxy works because it correctly passes the flag:

```
 Working (ADB proxy)                 Broken (rootcanal proxy)
      |                                    |
 --vhost_user_vsock=true             (flag missing)
      |                                    |
 VsockServer(cid=Some(3))           VsockServer(cid=None)
      |                                    |
 Unix socket:                        socket(AF_VSOCK, ...)
 /tmp/vsock_3_501/vm.vsock_5555          |
      |                              errno 19: ENODEV
   works on macOS                    SleepForever()
```

## Fix

Add `--vhost_user_vsock=` parameter to all four proxy commands in
`root_canal.cpp` (hci + test) and `netsim_server.cpp` (hci + test),
matching the pattern from `host/libs/config/adb/launch.cpp:144-145`.

The flag reads `instance_.vhost_user_vsock()` which is true when the
VM uses vhost-user vsock (always true on macOS, false on Linux with
kernel vsock).

This is backwards compatible with linux because the value will be false there.

Test Plan:
```
 . build/envsetup.sh && lunch aosp_cf_arm64_phone-userdebug && m out/host/darwin-x86/cvd-host_package.tar.gz
```
Rebuilt launch_cvd. Verified no more "Operation not supported" errors in launcher.log for rootcanal proxy on macOS.
